From ef494f03e926d2cf46b5a560491b206513d5b441 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:15:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Analyzer and feeds from the owner's list of 2026-10-28

Analyzer: no MLS note or "Nothing else to type" line on the form; a Needs work box under
Paying cash with an optional "I look for items that need repaired" field; the listing's photos
and description are read for repairs on every home (cached per listing) and shown with a cost
range only when work is seen, the midpoint going into Repairs; no Type/Beds/Baths row; the
narrative adds what the overview and flags leave out; Loan opens a second row in the same box
(down payment, rate, term, loan amount); Compare puts a second scenario beside the first with
the Chapter III bookmark between them (a First/Second bar on a phone); each ? says what is good
in that town; the similar homes row scrolls by itself and drags; Talk to an agent opens the
sitewide popup with the analyzed address.

Sitewide: every link to the contact page opens a name, phone and email popup that sends the
page's home; the static "call while reading" line is gone. Feeds: top vacation homes from
Cherry Grove to Pawleys Island on the second-home guide, homes near major employers on the jobs
guide, older and distressed homes east of 17 on fix and flip, "Top homes in" each town, and a
feed fitted to each HOA guide.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
